Z||000000||LoW_KeY||12-04-2001||10:41 PM||||Ok I'm just curious I'm looking to do a performance rebuild.<P>I was wondering what all is out there.. so far I have this in mind.<P>Mill heads<BR>Cam & roller rockers<BR>port polish<BR>balance<P>anything else? I'm not to engine inclined and plan on doing this myself with the help from my dads friend, he'll most likely be telling me what to do so I can get a base of what to do.. thanks.<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||12-04-2001||11:24 PM||||<BR>Ok I'm just curious I'm looking to do a performance rebuild.<P>I was wondering what all is out there.. so far I have this in mind.<P>Mill heads<BR>Cam & roller rockers<BR>port polish<BR>balance<P>Hey KC!<BR>First, get the heads rebuilt (valve job), but do not mill unless warped...<BR>If you want to bump compession ratio, change the pistons...<BR>The roller rockers are OK, but a roller cam and lifters is better...<BR>Port and polish, OK, but port matching (intake and exhaust) is better...<BR>Balance? I hope it all balances!!!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||erikred||12-05-2001||11:25 AM||||I strongly recommend getting a three angle valve job. It is just too much of an improvement to pass up while you are rebuilding anyway. Make sure they do the valves and the seats.<P>You may consider checking out Techline's high tech engine coatings. They have stuff that you can coat they internals with that gives better wear and power.<P>Erik-||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||12-05-2001||07:19 PM||||You can also have the intake extrude honed, don't forget bored out throttle body, K&N filter, headers, and flow thru cat and performance muffler. You can also remove the baffle from the air intake box. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
